From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:36:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ppu: a journal of one thread's guest stores
 (PS3RECOMP_STORE_JOURNAL)

For checking a hand-written replacement of a lifted function against the
lifted body: run one with the journal on, undo what it wrote, run the other,
and compare what each changed. Compiled in only with PS3RECOMP_STORE_JOURNAL
(a port's build option, off by default); without it the store paths and the
lifted code are what they were (PPU_DCBZ expands to the same memset, and
PPU_ST_DIAG to the same two globals).

While a thread journals (ppu_journal_begin), each guest store it makes is
noted before it lands, with the bytes it overwrites: vm_write8/16/32/64
through VM_WRITE_COH, ppu_stwcx32/ppu_stdcx64, and the lifted code's dcbz
(now emitted as PPU_DCBZ). The lifted code's inline stores reach vm_write*
while any thread journals: the store window and each function's store
snapshot close, as they do for the store watches (g_store_journal is folded
into the snapshot's key). Other threads' stores take the slow path too but
are not noted. Not covered: runtime code that writes guest memory with host
stores of its own (HLE, DMA, the RSX).

ppu_store_journal.h is header-only, so a host test builds it on its own
(the port's tools/tests/test_store_journal.sh). Written for the port; not
specific to the title (a candidate for upstream).
---
 runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp      |  30 +++++++-
 runtime/ppu/ppu_store_journal.h | 118 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/ppu_lifter.py             |  20 ++++--
 3 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 runtime/ppu/ppu_store_journal.h

